course: dictionary
lesson: 11302
title: Yawn: more than tiredness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A yawn is when you open your mouth very wide and breathe in deeply, usually because you are tired or bored. The word can also be a noun: «Yawns are catching, even reading about yawning can start one.» So a yawn is both the action and the thing you do.
explain: Look at the words around yawn to find its meaning. In «Tiredness shows as yawning, heavy eyes, clumsiness and a short temper», the other signs (heavy eyes, clumsiness) tell you yawning means tired. In «what a yawn», the phrase is a joke: something so dull that it makes you yawn.
explain: Yawning is a reflex, and it is catching. Seeing someone yawn often makes you yawn too, and dogs can catch yawns from their owners. Scientists still argue about why we yawn, so this is a good place to say, «I'm not sure, but I can read about it.»
fact: To yawn means to open your mouth very wide and breathe in deeply, usually because you are tired or bored.
fact: A yawn is the act of yawning, and it can be a noun: «a yawn».
fact: «Something boring can be called "a yawn".» So «what a yawn» means what a boring thing.
fact: A «yawning gap» or hole is very wide and open, not sleepy at all.
fact: Yawning is a reflex, and it is catching: seeing someone yawn can make you yawn too, even dogs.
exercise: Tiredness shows as which of these? | Running fast | A big laugh | Loud singing | *Yawning
exercise: «What a yawn», said Mo about the long film. What does a yawn mean here? | A loud noise | *Something boring | A big open mouth
exercise: «A yawning gap» in the fence is a gap that is what? | Hidden under leaves | Full of water | *Very wide and open | Very small
test: Why might you yawn when you see someone else yawn? | They are hungry and want food | *Yawning is catching, and it is a reflex | Yawns are only for dogs | You want to sing
test: What is the polite way to deal with a yawn in class? | Yawn very loudly at the teacher | *Cover your mouth with your hand | Shout loudly to let it out | Turn away and laugh
exam: What does «stifle a yawn» mean? | Sing a long note | *Hold back a yawn so it does not show | Yawn very loudly so everyone hears | Wake up suddenly
